  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\n$2 y y_{1}=3 x^{2}$\r\n$y_{1}=\\frac{3 x^{2}}{2 y} \\Rightarrow\\left(y_{1}\\right)_{m^{2}, m^{3}}=\\frac{3 \\times m^{4}}{2 \\times m^{3}}=\\frac{3 m}{2}$\r\nAgain; slope of normal $=-\\frac{2}{3 M}, m M=-\\frac{4}{9}$",
